# No co-authors

**TO NEVER COAUTHOR WORK AGAIN!**

Git commits must have a single author: the human who asked for the commit. Never attribute the agent, Cursor, Grok, Claude, or any tool as a co-author.

- Do not add `Co-authored-by` trailers (including Cursor, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, or any model name).
- Do not add `Signed-off-by` for the agent.
- Do not pass `--author`, `--trailer`, or any flag that changes authorship.
- Do not put "Generated by", "Assisted by", or similar in the commit message.
- After `git commit`, run `git log -1 --format=%B`. If a hook or Cursor injected `Co-authored-by`, do not push. Rewrite HEAD with `git commit-tree` and the human message only.
- Skill: `no-co-author` (`.claude/skills/no-co-author` and `.cursor/skills/no-co-author`).

The commit message is the human's. The author is the human's git identity.
